,{"text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/RootedTree","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/rootedtree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A tree with a root: an undirected ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parent(of:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"depth(of:)"},{"text":", and the queries tree algorithms start from. The vertices, edges and their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions are the tree’s; the root orders ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"text":" (each vertex’s incident edges in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position order, without the edge to its parent) and so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preorder"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"RootedTree","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-MutableDirectedGraph-Extensions":{"title":"Extensions to MutableDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-mutabledirectedgraph-extensions","abstract":[{"text":"Members other modules add to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-MutableDirectedGraph-Extensions","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent":{"title":"Grafluent","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent","abstract":[{"text":"A generic, high-performance graph library for Swift.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","iden